    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Subsequent annual wellness visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and a written prevention plan given to him and his caregiver. Depression and alcohol screens are negative. Cognition was assessed by direct observation in established mild dementia; the MoCA stays on the yearly dementia schedule. Ten-year cardiovascular risk is about 18 percent by the pooled cohort equations, from age alone, with no diabetes, hypertension, dyslipidemia, or smoking. [S]<list><item>Next annual wellness visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Mild dementia, type undetermined (F03.A0)</content>. Stable by observation and his caregiver&apos;s account. Heart rate 60 on donepezil 10 mg, without fainting or gastrointestinal effects. [S]<list><item>Continue donepezil 10 mg each morning.</item><item>Six-month dementia review in about six weeks.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Influenza vaccine, this season</td><td>Completed today</td><td>High-dose vaccine given today</td></tr><tr><td>Pneumococcal vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PCV20 given today; no further doses needed</td></tr><tr><td>Recombinant zoster vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Dose 1 given today; dose 2 due in two to six months</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine, this season</td><td>Due</td><td>Recommended at his age; his caregiver will arrange it at the pharmacy</td></tr><tr><td>RSV vaccine</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Recommended at 75 and older, and from 50 with conditions that raise risk; he has none. Review at 75</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis booster</td><td>Due</td><td>No dose on record in the past ten years; to be given with the second zoster dose</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 1; PHQ-9 continues at the dementia reviews</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol misuse screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C score 0</td></tr><tr><td>Cognitive assessment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Direct observation in established mild dementia; MoCA 19 at diagnosis, repeated yearly on the CMID schedule</td></tr><tr><td>Falls prevention</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Timed Up and Go 11 seconds; no falls; daily walking continues</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Whispered-voice test passed in both ears; hearing loss would worsen cognition, so it will be rechecked yearly</td></tr><tr><td>Eye examination</td><td>Due</td><td>No eye examination in the past two years; his caregiver will book one</td></tr><tr><td>Cholesterol screening and statin decision</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Total cholesterol 196, HDL 54, LDL 118, triglycerides 120 mg/dL. Ten-year risk about 18 percent from age alone, without diabetes, hypertension, dyslipidemia, or smoking, so the USPSTF criteria for a statin are not met. A statin was discussed; he prefers no new daily medicine, and his caregiver agrees</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Recommended for overweight adults 35 to 70; BMI 23.2, and glucose was normal in May</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>No screening on record in the past ten years; at 73 with mild dementia and good health, he chose a fecal immunochemical test, and a kit was given to his caregiver today</td></tr><tr><td>Prostate cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>PSA screening is not recommended at 70 and older</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time screening recommended for adults 18 to 79; no result on record; drawn with today&apos;s blood tests with his consent</td></tr><tr><td>Lung cancer and abdominal aortic aneurysm screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Never used tobacco</td></tr><tr><td>Advance care planning</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Health care agent named and his wishes recorded six weeks ago; reviewed today without change</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: High-dose influenza vaccine, 1895-1896 season; Pneumococcal conjugate vaccine PCV20; Recombinant zoster vaccine, dose 1 of 2 [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, Non-Alzheimer&apos;s dementia and Alzheimer&apos;s disease monographs (2026); Medicare Wellness Visits (Medicare Learning Network) (2026); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Six-month dementia review in about six weeks. Second zoster dose and the Tdap booster in two to six months. Return the stool test kit within two weeks; the hepatitis C result will be sent by letter. Next annual wellness visit in one year. Next scheduled visit 1895-10-27: six-month dementia review. [S]</paragraph></text>

